{
  "comment": [
    "Labelled ground truth. Every scenario is a full entity snapshot plus the",
    "event that triggered the decision, and the answers a competent human would",
    "give. These labels are the oracle: verify grades the engine against them,",
    "so a wrong label is worse than a missing scenario.",
    "",
    "The set is synthetic but shaped like a real house. Entity ids and state",
    "values follow Home Assistant conventions, so porting a scenario to the real",
    "instance is a copy, not a translation.",
    "",
    "Two properties worth preserving when editing:",
    "  - Every option in questions.json must appear often enough to be gradeable.",
    "    An option with one scenario tells you nothing about accuracy on it.",
    "  - Keep the deliberate negative cases. s14, s17 and s23 are normal life that",
    "    an eager engine misreads as an emergency, and they are what the",
    "    false-alarm ceiling in verify actually measures.",
    "",
    "entities is the full snapshot pushed into HA. event names the entity that",
    "changed, which is what an HA automation would pass as its trigger."
  ],
